# Context override that branches below the root — a recorded besluit-6 flank

Besluit 6 lowers a caller override of a `context` variable to a **chain** of
plain-rung top rungs above the callee's own ladder. When the override itself
is a **below-root branching** tree (a base rung carrying a nested exception
sub-group — the ch. 7.9 shape) it is not a plain-rung chain: only a chain of
plain-rung overrides lowers to top rungs, so the branching override stays
refused loudly, one of the narrowed remnants of the old blanket context
refusal (CONSTRUCTS row 9 / `spec/proposals/PHASE5-CATALA.md` decision 6).

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  context drempel content integer
  output uitkomst content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition drempel equals 10
  definition uitkomst equals grondslag - drempel

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslag content integer
  input a content boolean
  input b content boolean
  input c content boolean
  kamer scope Kamer
  output heffing content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition kamer.grondslag equals grondslag
  label basis definition kamer.drempel equals 5
  label lvl1 exception basis definition kamer.drempel
    under condition a consequence equals 20
  exception lvl1 definition kamer.drempel
    under condition b consequence equals 25
  exception lvl1 definition kamer.drempel
    under condition c consequence equals 30
  definition heffing equals kamer.uitkomst
```
